[SIZE="3"][COLOR="Yellow"]Info[/COLOR][/SIZE]
This library is for [U]addon developers[/U]. Download it, if an addon dependency tells you so.

[SIZE="3"][COLOR="DarkOrange"]Description[/COLOR][/SIZE]
This library is written to overcome one way to get the "Access a private function XYZ from insecure code" error. Beyond that it adds features the built-in menu does not have:
[LIST]
[*]Beginning with version 2.0: sub menus
[*]Beginning with version 3.0: dividers
[*]Beginning with version 5.0: checkboxes in sub menus
[*]Beginning with version 6.2: hooks into the inventory context menu and the key strip
[*]Beginning with version 6.8: tooltips for menu entries
[*]Beginning with version 6.9: alternative context menus using the keyboard modifier keys
[*]Beginning with version 7.0: headers
[*]Beginning with version 7.1: hooks into the player, guild roster, friends list, group list and ignore list context menus
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][COLOR="DarkOrange"]Background[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Controls, created from add-on code (as part of the code path) are marked as "insecure/compromised".
Functions, which have no problem with being called from "insecure" controls, are still working perfectly.
Like those of add-ons or [B]Show On Map[/B], [B]Link in Chat[/B] or [B]Get Help[/B].
But "secured" functions like [B]UseItem[/B], [B]InitiateDestroy[/B], [B]PickupInventoryItem[/B] raise the error message from above.
Once you hook [B]AddMenuItem[/B] ALL controls created for the context-menu are "insecure".

Prior to ESO 2.0.13 if an add-on offers a full custom context-menu (no built-in menu entries) and this context-menu is shown first after (re-)load UI the first menu item controls are insecure. A crash of "Use" in the inventory afterwards was guaranteed.
Starting with ESO 2.0.13 ZOS preallocates 10 "secure" menu items. See [URL="http://www.esoui.com/forums/showpost.php?p=21915&postcount=50"]here[/URL].
But this just reduces the chance of running into that problem, it does not fix it.
Currently the number of preallocated controls is 30. Running into this problem with AddMenuItem is really rare, but inventory action slots still don't like custom menu entries.

To avoid the error message, the controls of built-in menu items and add-on menu items must be strictly separated. That's what [B]AddCustomMenuItem[/B] of this library does. It uses its own pool of controls, which look exactly the same. Sounds strange, but works.

[SIZE="3"][COLOR="DarkOrange"]I don't use private functions. Why should I use this lib?[/COLOR][/SIZE]
It's not you, who uses private functions. It is built-in code, which re-uses controls indirectly created by your add-on in AddMenuItem.

[SIZE="3"][COLOR="DarkOrange"]I want to use this lib, so what to do?[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Add [FONT="Courier New"]LibCustomMenu[/FONT] to the [FONT="Courier New"]## DependsOn:[/FONT] line of your add-on manifest. The library is available as the global variable [FONT="Courier New"]LibCustomMenu[/FONT]. (LibStub is no longer supported since version 7.0.)
Then do a text search for the global function AddMenuItem (not any :AddMenuItem of other objects) and replace it with AddCustomMenuItem.
Be careful with a simple "Replace All" over all files! You probably replace the AddMenuItem of LibCustomMenu itself ;)

[SIZE="2"][COLOR="DarkOrange"]Version 1.0[/COLOR][/SIZE]
[URL="http://www.esoui.com/forums/attachment.php?attachmentid=594&d=1430285148"]This version[/URL] was intended as proof of concept, but was successfully used in Beartram's FCO Item Saver, Circonian's FilterIt and my Fish Fillet.

[SIZE="2"][COLOR="DarkOrange"]Version 2.0[/COLOR][/SIZE]
In order to have more value than avoiding a rare, just annoying "bug", sirinsidiator suggested and provided proof of concept code for sub menu items.
A big thank to sirinsidiator!
I finalized it and here we are.

[SIZE="3"][COLOR="DarkOrange"]Overview[/COLOR][/SIZE]
[B]Create your own menus[/B] (use together with ClearMenu() and ShowMenu())
[LIST]
[*]AddCustomMenuItem(mytext, myfunction, itemType, myfont, normalColor, highlightColor, itemYPad) - API 2.0, 3.0, 5.0, 7.0
[*]AddCustomSubMenuItem(mytext, entries, myfont, normalColor, highlightColor, itemYPad, subMenuButtonCallbackFunc) - API 2.0, 3.0, 5.0, 6.8, 7.0
[*]AddCustomMenuTooltip(tooltip, index) - API 6.8
[/LIST]
[B]Hook into existing menus[/B] (function names are called on the library: LibCustomMenu:RegisterXyz(func, category))
[LIST]
[*][B]RegisterContextMenu[/B](func, category) - Inventory slot, right click. API 6.2
Signature: func(inventorySlot, slotActions)
[*][B]RegisterKeyStripEnter[/B](func, category) - Inventory slot, mouse hover (key strip). API 6.2
Signature: func(inventorySlot, slotActions)
[*][B]RegisterKeyStripExit[/B](func) - Inventory slot, mouse exit. API 6.2
Signature: func()
[*][B]RegisterSpecialKeyContextMenu[/B](func) - Inventory slot, right click + modifier key. API 6.9
Signature: func(inventorySlot, slotActions, ctrl, alt, shift, command)
[*][B]RegisterPlayerContextMenu[/B](func, category) - Chat player link. API 6.92
Signature: func(playerName, rawName)
[*][B]RegisterGuildRosterContextMenu[/B](func, category) - Guild roster member. API 7.1
Signature: func(rowData)
[*][B]RegisterFriendsListContextMenu[/B](func, category) - Friends list. API 7.2
Signature: func(rowData)
[*][B]RegisterGroupListContextMenu[/B](func, category) - Group list. API 7.2
Signature: func(rowData)
[*][B]RegisterIgnoreListContextMenu[/B](func, category) - Ignore list. API 7.3
Signature: func(rowData)
[/LIST]
The player, guild roster, friends, group and ignore list hooks are not active on console.

[SIZE="3"][COLOR="DarkOrange"]API 2.0[/COLOR][/SIZE]
function AddCustomMenuItem(mytext, myfunction, itemType, myfont, normalColor, highlightColor, itemYPad)

Fully compatible with AddMenuItem.
mytext: string, required. Caption of menu item.
myfunction: function(), required. Called if clicked.
itemType: int, optional. MENU_ADD_OPTION_LABEL or MENU_ADD_OPTION_CHECKBOX (and MENU_ADD_OPTION_HEADER since API 7.0). Default MENU_ADD_OPTION_LABEL.
myfont: string, optional.
normalColor: ZO_ColorDef, optional. Color of unselected item.
highlightColor: ZO_ColorDef, optional. Color of selected/hovered item.
itemYPad: int, optional. y-padding between items.


function AddCustomSubMenuItem(mytext, entries, myfont, normalColor, highlightColor, itemYPad, subMenuButtonCallbackFunc)

mytext: string, required. Caption of menu item.
entries: table of sub items or callback returning table of sub items, required. A callback is evaluated every time the sub menu opens.
myfont: string, optional. Default font of the sub items.
normalColor: ZO_ColorDef, optional. Color of unselected/normal sub item.
highlightColor: ZO_ColorDef, optional. Color of selected/hovered sub item.
itemYPad: int, optional. y-padding between sub items.
subMenuButtonCallbackFunc: function, optional. Callback function for the click on the submenu open button (the one at the main menu showing the submenu). The menu is closed before it is called. (Since version 7.0.1)

sub item:
label: string or function(rootMenu, childControl), required.
callback: function(), required.
disabled: boolean or function(rootMenu, childControl), optional. Default false. if true, sub item is visible, but gray and not clickable.
visible: boolean or function(rootMenu, childControl), optional. Default true.

[COLOR="Yellow"]These examples are for self-created menus. If you want to add items to the inventory context-menu, look at the example for LibCustomMenu:RegisterContextMenu more below.[/COLOR]

example 1:
[highlight="Lua"]local entries = {
  {
    label = "Test 1",
    callback = function() d("Test 1") end,
  },
  {
    label = "Test 2",
    callback = function() d("Test 2") end,
    disabled = function(rootMenu, childControl) return true end,
  }
}
ClearMenu()
AddCustomSubMenuItem("Sub Menu", entries)
ShowMenu()[/highlight]

example 2:
[highlight="Lua"]local function GetEntries(rootMenu)
d("run")
return {
  {
    label = function() return GetTimeStamp() end,
    callback = function() d("Test 1") end,
  },
  {
    label = "Test 2",
    callback = function() d("Test 2") end,
    disabled = function(rootMenu, childControl) return true end,
  }
}
end
ClearMenu()
AddCustomSubMenuItem("Sub Menu", GetEntries)
ShowMenu()[/highlight]
If you have Notebook or ZAM Notebook, you could copy&paste the scripts from above and execute them.

[SIZE="3"][COLOR="DarkOrange"]API 3.0[/COLOR][/SIZE]
In addition to API 2.0:
Allow divider by setting member [B]label[/B] to a static "-". Suggested by Beartram. You can use [FONT="Courier New"]LibCustomMenu.DIVIDER[/FONT] for better readability.
Dividers also work at the top level: [FONT="Courier New"]AddCustomMenuItem("-")[/FONT].
Dividers at the beginning or the end of a menu and multiple dividers in a row are hidden automatically.

example:
[highlight="Lua"]local entries = {
  {
    label = "Test 1",
    callback = function() d("Test 1") end,
  },
  {
    label = "-",
  },
  {
    label = "Test 2",
    callback = function() d("Test 2") end,
    disabled = function(rootMenu, childControl) return true end,
  }
}
ClearMenu()
AddCustomSubMenuItem("Sub Menu", entries)
ShowMenu()[/highlight]

[SIZE="3"][COLOR="DarkOrange"]API 4.1[/COLOR][/SIZE]
In addition to API 3.0:
actionSlots:AddCustomSlotAction(actionStringId, actionCallback, actionType, visibilityFunction, options)

[strike]for example while hooking ZO_InventorySlot_DiscoverSlotActionsFromActionList(inventorySlot, slotActions)[/strike]
for example within the callback of API 6.2. See below.

[SIZE="3"][COLOR="DarkOrange"]API 5.0[/COLOR][/SIZE]
In addition to API 4.1+:
New entry properties [FONT="Courier New"]itemType[/FONT] and [FONT="Courier New"]checked[/FONT].
itemType = MENU_ADD_OPTION_LABEL (default) or MENU_ADD_OPTION_CHECKBOX for a checkbox
checked  = false/true or function() return state end
The initial checked state when opening the sub menu.
The callback of a checkbox entry receives the new state as parameter: function(state).

example:
[highlight="Lua"]local myState = true
    local entries = {
      {
        label = "Test 1",
        callback = function(state) myState = state df("Test 1: %s", tostring(myState)) end,
        checked = function() return myState end,
        itemType = MENU_ADD_OPTION_CHECKBOX,
      },
      {
        label = "Test 1b",
        callback = function() d("Test 1b") end,
        itemType = MENU_ADD_OPTION_LABEL,
      },
      {
        label = "-",
      },
      {
        label = "Test 2",
        callback = function() d("Test 2") end,
        disabled = function(rootMenu, childControl) return true end,
      }
    }
    ClearMenu()
    AddCustomSubMenuItem("Sub Menu", entries)
    ShowMenu()[/highlight]

[SIZE="3"][COLOR="DarkOrange"]API 6.2[/COLOR][/SIZE]
In addition to API 5+:
Added callbacks, you can register to, to hook into inventory slot context menu. You don't need to reinvent the hook and are able to control the position of your entry/entries more granular.

category
lib.CATEGORY_EARLY
lib.CATEGORY_PRIMARY
lib.CATEGORY_SECONDARY
lib.CATEGORY_TERTIARY
lib.CATEGORY_QUATERNARY
lib.CATEGORY_LATE

CATEGORY_EARLY is before the first built-in menu entry.
CATEGORY_PRIMARY is after the first built-in menu entry. And so on.
CATEGORY_LATE is after built-in menu and default.

lib:RegisterContextMenu(func, category)
Register to the context menu of the inventory mouse right click.

lib:RegisterKeyStripEnter(func, category)
Register to the inventory mouse hover used to update the keybind buttons at the bottom.

func: callback function to be called.
Signature:
[highlight="Lua"]local function func(inventorySlot, slotActions)
end[/highlight]

category: optional. defaults to CATEGORY_LATE.

lib:RegisterKeyStripExit(func)
Register to the inventory mouse hover used to update the keybind buttons at the bottom, if the mouse exits an inventory slot.

func: callback function to be called.
Signature:
[highlight="Lua"]local function func()
end[/highlight]

example:
[highlight="Lua"]ZO_CreateStringId("SI_BINDING_NAME_SHOW_POPUP", "Show in Popup")
local function AddItem(inventorySlot, slotActions)
  local valid = ZO_Inventory_GetBagAndIndex(inventorySlot)
  if not valid then return end
  slotActions:AddCustomSlotAction(SI_BINDING_NAME_SHOW_POPUP, function()
    local bagId, slotIndex = ZO_Inventory_GetBagAndIndex(inventorySlot)
    local itemLink = GetItemLink(bagId, slotIndex)
    ZO_PopupTooltip_SetLink(itemLink)
  end , "")
end

LibCustomMenu:RegisterContextMenu(AddItem, LibCustomMenu.CATEGORY_PRIMARY)
[/highlight]

example 2:
[highlight="Lua"]local function AddItem(inventorySlot, slotActions)
  local bagId, slotIndex = ZO_Inventory_GetBagAndIndex(inventorySlot)
  if not CanItemBePlayerLocked(bagId, slotIndex) then return end
  local locked = IsItemPlayerLocked(bagId, slotIndex)

  slotActions:AddCustomSlotAction(locked and SI_ITEM_ACTION_UNMARK_AS_LOCKED or SI_ITEM_ACTION_MARK_AS_LOCKED, function()
    SetItemIsPlayerLocked(bagId, slotIndex, not locked)
  end, "keybind2")
  -- you can use: "primary", "secondary", "keybind1", "keybind2"
end

local menu = LibCustomMenu
--menu:RegisterContextMenu(AddItem, menu.CATEGORY_PRIMARY)
menu:RegisterKeyStripEnter(AddItem, menu.CATEGORY_LATE)
[/highlight]
Not really practical, because it hides the built-in keybind. :)
But you could use the callback just to be notified as well.

[SIZE="3"][COLOR="DarkOrange"]API 6.8[/COLOR][/SIZE]
In addition to API 6.2+:
Added functionality to add an optional tooltip to a menu entry.
For the top level menu entries there is a new global function:
function AddCustomMenuTooltip(tooltip, index)
tooltip: Either a string shown as a simple tooltip or a callback function to let you do everything.
Signature:
[highlight="Lua"]local function func(control, inside)
end[/highlight]
control: the menu entry control.
inside: The function is called on mouse enter with inside=true and on mouse exit with inside=false.

index: Optional. Index of the menu entry, the tooltip is for. By default the index of the last added item is used. => You call AddCustomMenuItem and then AddCustomMenuTooltip.

For sub-menus a new key "tooltip" can be used. Again it is either a string or the callback function with the signature from above.

example:
[highlight="Lua"]
    local myState = true
    local entries = {
      {
        label = "Test 1",
        callback = function(state) myState = state df("Test 1: %s", tostring(myState)) end,
        checked = function() return myState end,
        itemType = MENU_ADD_OPTION_CHECKBOX,
        tooltip = "This is Test 1",
      },
      {
        label = "Test 1b",
        callback = function() d("Test 1b") end,
        itemType = MENU_ADD_OPTION_LABEL,
        tooltip = "This is Test 1b",
      },
      {
        label = "-",
      },
      {
        label = "Test 2",
        callback = function() d("Test 2") end,
        disabled = function(rootMenu, childControl) return true end,
      }
    }
    ClearMenu()
    AddCustomSubMenuItem("Sub Menu", entries)
    AddCustomMenuTooltip("A sub-menu")
    AddCustomMenuItem("-", function() d("soso") end)
    AddCustomMenuItem("Button", function() d("jojo") end)
    AddCustomMenuTooltip(function(control, inside) if inside then d("A great button") end end)
    AddCustomMenuItem("CheckBox", function() d("soso") end, MENU_ADD_OPTION_CHECKBOX)
    ShowMenu()[/highlight]
[COLOR="DarkOrange"][SIZE="2"]How to use Checkbox at top level[/SIZE][/COLOR]
[highlight="Lua"]local index = AddCustomMenuItem("CheckBox", function() <your callback> end, MENU_ADD_OPTION_CHECKBOX)
if needToCheckIt then
    ZO_CheckButton_SetChecked(ZO_Menu.items[index].checkbox)
end[/highlight]

[COLOR="DarkOrange"][SIZE="3"]API 6.9[/SIZE][/COLOR]
lib:EnableSpecialKeyContextMenu(key)
key: KEY_CTRL or KEY_ALT or KEY_SHIFT or KEY_COMMAND
Show an alternative context menu, if the special key is pressed while right-clicking the inventory item.

lib:RegisterSpecialKeyContextMenu(func)
Register a callback for the alternative context menu. You, the addon author, have to check which menu items you want to add for the given combination of special keys. (See signature below)
You have to enable all the keys you want to handle. See lib:EnableSpecialKeyContextMenu(key). There is no DisableSpecialKeyContextMenu, because you don't know who else had enabled them.
If one of the enabled keys is pressed, the custom entries come from the callbacks registered with RegisterSpecialKeyContextMenu instead of the ones registered with RegisterContextMenu.

Signature:
[highlight="Lua"]local function func(inventorySlot, slotActions, ctrl, alt, shift, command)
end[/highlight]

example:
[highlight="Lua"]local menu = LibCustomMenu
menu:EnableSpecialKeyContextMenu(KEY_SHIFT)
menu:RegisterSpecialKeyContextMenu(function(inventorySlot, slotActions, ctrl, alt, shift, command)
  if not shift then return end
  slotActions:AddCustomSlotAction(SI_BINDING_NAME_SHOW_POPUP, function() d("Shift + right click") end, "")
end)[/highlight]

[COLOR="DarkOrange"][SIZE="3"]API 6.92[/SIZE][/COLOR]
lib:RegisterPlayerContextMenu(func, category)
Register to the context menu of the chat player link mouse right click,

func: callback function to be called.
Signature:
[code]
local function func(playerName, rawName)
end
[/code]

Category: See API 6.2 description for the available categories.

[COLOR="DarkOrange"][SIZE="3"]API 7.0[/SIZE][/COLOR]
In addition to API 6.x:
New menu item type [FONT="Courier New"]MENU_ADD_OPTION_HEADER[/FONT]. A header is a non-clickable caption in a bigger font, with a divider line below. It can be used at the top level and as [FONT="Courier New"]itemType[/FONT] of a sub item. The default font is [FONT="Courier New"]LibCustomMenu.headerFont[/FONT] ("ZoFontWinH3").
The callback of a sub menu item may return [B]true[/B] to keep the sub menu open (otherwise the whole menu is closed after the click). Use this to refresh other items of the sub menu.
The properties [FONT="Courier New"]myfont[/FONT], [FONT="Courier New"]normalColor[/FONT] and [FONT="Courier New"]highlightColor[/FONT] can also be set per sub item, either as value or as function(rootMenu, childControl). They override the values given to AddCustomSubMenuItem.

example:
[highlight="Lua"]ClearMenu()
AddCustomMenuItem("My Header", nil, MENU_ADD_OPTION_HEADER)
AddCustomSubMenuItem("Sub Menu", {
  { label = "Section", itemType = MENU_ADD_OPTION_HEADER },
  { label = "Test 1", callback = function() d("Test 1") end },
})
ShowMenu()[/highlight]

[COLOR="DarkOrange"][SIZE="3"]API 7.1[/SIZE][/COLOR]
lib:RegisterGuildRosterContextMenu(func, category)
Register to the context menu of the guild roster member mouse right click.

func: callback function to be called.
Signature:
[code]
local function func(rowData)
end
[/code]

[COLOR="DarkOrange"][SIZE="3"]API 7.2[/SIZE][/COLOR]
lib:RegisterFriendsListContextMenu(func, category)
Register to the context menu of the friends list mouse right click.

lib:RegisterGroupListContextMenu(func, category)
Register to the context menu of the group list mouse right click.

Both analog to RegisterGuildRosterContextMenu. See above.

[COLOR="DarkOrange"][SIZE="3"]API 7.3[/SIZE][/COLOR]
lib:RegisterIgnoreListContextMenu(func, category)
Register to the context menu of the ignore list mouse right click.
Analog to RegisterGuildRosterContextMenu. See above.

[COLOR="DarkOrange"][SIZE="2"]Example[/SIZE][/COLOR]
[highlight="Lua"]local function AddItem(data)
  AddCustomMenuItem("Example", function() d(data.displayName) end)
end

local menu = LibCustomMenu
menu:RegisterFriendsListContextMenu(AddItem, menu.CATEGORY_EARLY)
menu:RegisterFriendsListContextMenu(AddItem, menu.CATEGORY_LATE)[/highlight]

[SIZE="3"][COLOR="DarkOrange"]For other libraries[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Since version 7.2.2 [FONT="Courier New"]LibCustomMenu.AddMenuItem[/FONT] and [FONT="Courier New"]LibCustomMenu.AddSubMenuItem[/FONT] are available as hook-points for LibScrollableMenu.

